mmary of what was created:\n\n## Regex Pattern Explanation\n\nThe regex in `/app/regex.txt` matches dates in YYYY-MM-DD format appearing in lines that contain an IPv4 address, capturing only the last date if multiple exist.\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 Validation** (without leading zeros):\n   - Each octet: `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])` matches 0-255\n   - Word boundaries: `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9.])` and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9.])` prevent adjacent alphanumerics/dots\n\n2. **Date Validation** (YYYY-MM-DD):\n   - Year: `\\d{4}` (any 4 digits)\n   - Months with 31 days (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): days 01-31\n   - Months with 30 days (04,06,09,11): days 01-30  \n   - February (02): days 01-29 (as per requirement)\n\n3. **Last Date Only**:\n   - Lookahead `(?=.*IPv4...)` confirms IPv4 exists on line\n   - Greedy `.*` consumes characters up to the last date\n   - Capturing group extracts only the final date\n\n**Usage with Python:**\n```python\nimport re\n\nwith open(\"/app/regex.txt\") as f:\n    pattern = f.read().strip()\n\nmatches = re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)\n# Returns list of captured dates from qualifying lines\n```\n\nAll 10 verification tests pass, including edge cases for valid/invalid dates, word boundaries, and multiple dates on single lines.","ttft_ms":138577,"type":"result","duration_ms":190996,"uuid":"1450f7e6-d5b3-4a60-9cdc-033d53eb9e4e","ttft_stream_ms":1138,"time_to_request_ms":75,"queued_turn_count":0}
